"The Art'h Residence is the home of the Primary's family, the Art'hs, in Knight Rapport 1."
"It has no guards or walls."
"Small pentagonal mirrored buildings with flat leaf-covered roofs dot its grounds."
"Their mirrors reflect everything but Alden, and their doors fade from mirror to wood and slide."
"One outbuilding is a training space for meditation, dance and martial arts, with a tocking beat."
"The main house is built around several giant trees and rises three or more stories."
"Rooms connect to rooms, with seating nooks, bookcases, a fire pit, plush rugs and candlelight."
"The formal dining room is the largest space; staff cook in an ultra-modern kitchen."
"Upstairs a long hall of numbered doors splits around a tree trunk behind floor-to-ceiling glass."
"Many wizards, knights and children live there, and the Art'hs eat three meals a day."
"Murmur, a mleirt, wanders every room tidying and sniffing the residents."
"Knight instructor Rel-art'h lives behind door seven; Stuart's room is at the end of the hall."
"Stuart's room is nearly bare, with a standing desk and a hidden window onto the forest."
"Staff sign a Privacy of the House contract not to share what they learn there."
"A large summonarium, almost as big as LeafSong's, is down a long winding path."
"The Mother sent Alden near there so the Art'hs could execute him if repair went wrong."
"It is the house of Jeneth-art'h, the Primary, a siblinghold he founded with Alis and Tesen."
"The summonarium's design is painted on stone beneath three dark trees whose limbs form a roof."
"Cone-shaped hanging baskets big enough to sit in hang high in the trees, with no ladders."
"Many cottage-sized outbuildings serve as houses and offices; only foot-worn paths join them."
"Stuart's favorite guest cottage sits by the stream, its mirrored door sliding open to a hand."
"Guest cottages hold a bowl of welcome, tea, cigars and weak one-use magic rings."
"The en family, long dear and trusted neighbors, live across the stream."
"Zansees, glittering water bugs, light the stream at night and are jarred as decoration."
"The main house has a narrow solarium, an open cold alcove kitchen and a big living room."
"A husenot room shows living rock-like animals under a transparent floor."
"A below-ground supply library holds rare ingredients, weapons and a giant tree root."
"A manuscript library with portraits and marriage contracts is above the supply library."
"Olorn-art'h, a potter-wizard spouse of Jeneth, works in a cottage with a basin of magic mud."
"Staff families have served the art'h wizards and knights for generations."
"Only a hn'tyon can declare someone a guest there; guests are exempt from Privacy of the House."
"Stuart invited Alden as his first guest in the art'h house."
"A mudroom off the entry holds footwear, outerwear and a table for gifts."
"An enchanted hearthstone is lit with a drop of Artonan blood, honoring kinship with the Mother."
"A formal wevvi room is a circle where the host serves wevvi from a cart."
"The School Cottage is on the grounds; Rel-art'h teaches at the Rapport school."
"Guest cottages have showers with many settings and rings for convenience spells."
"A forest clearing near the house holds tables of different materials for brewing."
"The cottage of oaths is where household members prepare for knight oaths."
"A forest training site with a big base tree is a hike from the summonarium."
"The art'h summonarium is larger than the Rapport School's."
"All of Stuart's siblings were born under one tree on the grounds."
"Sina's tree, a young tree in the forest, marks where she chose her first binding."
"The Streamview cottage, a guest cottage over the zansee stream, has triangular ceiling tiles."
"Other Alden, Stuart's pet ryeh-b't, has a room of its own in the house."
"A heated outdoor bathing pool runs along the stream through the trees."
"Beyond the last buildings the stream falls over a small ledge into a pool."
"The land was ravaged by a massive corruption event long ago; the dark-barked trees survived."
"The Primary's wizard ancestors nourished the trees and buried their dead beneath them."
"Old belief holds that souls travel the roots to the Mother's heart."
"The manuscript library holds art, memories and learning tools along dark shelved corridors."
"The grounds include an o'odee field."
